<title>INDIA: Delhi bourse union calls off planned strike.</title>
<headline>Delhi bourse union calls off planned strike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A planned one-day strike on Tuesday by workers at the Delhi Stock Exchange has been called off, a labour leader said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Delhi Stock Exchange Karamcharis (workers) Union called off the strike after the bourse's management accepted some of the union'sr demands, its general secretary, Satyawan Singh, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said the management had agreed to raise house rent allowance and dearness (cost of living) allowance for the bourse's workers.</p>
</text>
